    - "#c2703d"
    - "#4a7a5c"
  metrics:
    radius: 2
---

# House style

A custom theme is an override, not a replacement. `extends: default` names the
theme it starts from and the rest of the map is a patch: the tokens listed here
win, every token not listed keeps the value the base gave it, and the marks,
status colours and scheme all come through untouched. A document that wants
one different grey should have to write one line, not restate a palette.

The palette is the exception to the patching rule. `categorical` is assigned in
fixed order and never cycled, so a partial list would silently change which
series got which colour; it replaces the base's list outright, and with it the
base's validation verdict, because a verdict about a palette says nothing about
a different one.

```mdv line
title: Signups by plan
x: month
y: [free, pro, team]
---
month,free,pro,team
2026-03,410,120,44
2026-04,438,141,52
2026-05,402,168,61
2026-06,455,183,58
```

Three series reach the three colours the front matter named, the gridlines and
the value labels reach the overridden tokens, and every piece of text is set in
the overridden family at the overridden size — which is what makes this a
render case rather than a parse one. A theme that resolves but never reaches
the marks has not been applied.
